sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User (Web or Desktop)
    participant Client as Client Application
    participant Gateway as API Gateway / Rate Limiter
    participant AuthService as Identity & Auth Service
    participant PasswordEngine as Argon2id Engine
    participant Database as PostgreSQL Database
    participant Redis as Redis Session Store

    Note over User,Client: Registration Flow: STRICTLY NO EMAIL VERIFICATION GATE
    User->>Client: Enters email and password (min 15 chars)
    Client->>Client: Client-side validation (regex, length >= 15)<br/>Displays warning: "Email is self-asserted & unverified"
    Client->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/register { email, password, displayName }
    
    Gateway->>Gateway: Check IP /24 rate limit (Max 5 / hour)
    alt Rate Limit Exceeded
        Gateway-->>Client: HTTP 429 Too Many Requests (Retry-After)
        Client-->>User: Display rate limit alert
    else Allowed
        Gateway->>AuthService: Forward registration payload
        AuthService->>Database: Query existing user by normalized email
        alt Email Already Registered
            AuthService->>PasswordEngine: Dummy Argon2id hash (Normalize timing)
            AuthService-->>Gateway: HTTP 409 Conflict (Generic error format)
            Gateway-->>Client: HTTP 409 Conflict ("Registration failed")
            Client-->>User: Display generic error message
        else Email Available
            AuthService->>PasswordEngine: Hash password (Argon2id: m=64MB, t=3, p=4)
            PasswordEngine-->>AuthService: Return password_hash
            AuthService->>Database: INSERT into users (email, password_hash, status='active')
            AuthService->>Database: INSERT into user_profiles (display_name, locale, timezone)
            
            Note over AuthService: CRITICAL: ZERO verification email or token generated
            
            AuthService->>AuthService: Generate 128-bit CSPRNG session token
            AuthService->>Database: INSERT into sessions (user_id, token_hash, client_type)
            AuthService->>Redis: Cache session token (TTL: 24h/7d)
            
            AuthService-->>Gateway: HTTP 201 Created (User Profile + Session Cookie / Tokens)
            Gateway-->>Client: HTTP 201 Created
            Client-->>User: Account active immediately; redirect to Dashboard
        end
    end
